From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pavel Demyanov <greypax@cybergusli.ai>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:50:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Wait for a new thread to start before returning
 it.

On iOS the server suspends a thread through Mach, and a thread suspended
before its init_thread request reached the server never runs. Half-Life 2
creates its worker threads suspended and suspends each one again at once
to read its context; the one whose init came after that stayed parked,
and the engine waited 60 s for it ("Thread failed to initialize") with a
black screen. The server learns a thread's TEB from init_thread, so
CreateRemoteThreadEx in the current process waits, up to about a second,
until ThreadBasicInformation shows it.

Built for i386 only, the scope tested in Half-Life 2: 64-bit programs
keep Wine's behaviour.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-25-touchpad-build.md
Offered-upstream: no; Mach thread suspension is the iOS port's
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/kernelbase/thread.c | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/thread.c b/dlls/kernelbase/thread.c
index 92ef073..3dd7162 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/thread.c
@@ -79,6 +79,35 @@ struct _PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_LIST
     struct proc_thread_attr attrs[];
 };
 
+/* Playport: the new thread's own start before the caller may suspend it.
+ *
+ * On iOS the server suspends a thread through Mach. A thread suspended
+ * before its init_thread request has reached the server never runs:
+ * Half-Life 2 creates its worker threads suspended and suspends each one
+ * again at once to read its context, and the one whose init came after that
+ * suspension stayed parked, so the engine waited 60 s for it ("Thread failed
+ * to initialize") with a black screen. The server learns the thread's TEB
+ * from init_thread, so the creator waits, up to about a second, until
+ * ThreadBasicInformation shows it. */
+#ifdef __i386__
+static void wait_thread_started( HANDLE handle )
+{
+    THREAD_BASIC_INFORMATION info;
+    LARGE_INTEGER delay;
+    unsigned int i;
+
+    delay.QuadPart = -10000; /* 1 ms */
+    for (i = 0; i < 1000; i++)
+    {
+        if (NtQueryInformationThread( handle, ThreadBasicInformation, &info, sizeof(info), NULL )) return;
+        if (info.TebBaseAddress) return;
+        if (i < 16) NtYieldExecution();
+        else NtDelayExecution( FALSE, &delay );
+    }
+}
+#endif
+
+
 /***************************************************************************
  *           CreateRemoteThreadEx   (kernelbase.@)
  */
@@ -157,6 +186,9 @@ HANDLE WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH CreateRemoteThreadEx( HANDLE process, SECURITY_A
         RtlReleaseActivationContext( actctx );
     }
 
+#ifdef __i386__
+    if (process == GetCurrentProcess()) wait_thread_started( handle );
+#endif
     if (id) *id = HandleToULong( client_id.UniqueThread );
     if (!(flags & CREATE_SUSPENDED)) NtResumeThread( handle, &ret );
     return handle;
